<%# Single-line limits banner: slot usage + refresh cadence + upgrade CTA
    for plans that lack Apple Ads popularity. Replaced by Turbo Stream
    after create/destroy to keep the slot count accurate. Callers pass
    the precomputed `usage` count so this partial doesn't need to hit the
    DB for that -- the parent view/Turbo Stream already knows the slot count.

    Task 24 addition: when an org has TrackedKeywordCountry rows with
    enabled=false (caused by a plan downgrade), surface the paused count
    and an "Upgrade to resume" CTA inline. Paused rows are excluded from
    `usage` in callers (which count enabled TKCs), so this is additive.

    Optional `estimate` local (Aso::NextCheckEstimator::Estimate) appends
    a "Next run <ETA>" segment; callers that don't pass it keep the old
    behaviour. %>
<%# locals: app, entitlements, usage, estimate (optional) %>
<% estimate ||= local_assigns[:estimate] %>
<% paused_count = TrackedKeywordCountry
                    .joins(:tracked_keyword)
                    .where(tracked_keywords: { apple_app_id: app.id, enabled: true })
                    .where(tracked_keyword_countries: { enabled: false })
                    .count %>
<div id="tracked-keywords-limits" class="text-xs text-base-content/55 mb-3">
  <%= usage %> of <%= entitlements.max_tracked_keywords_per_app %> keyword-country slots used &middot;
  <%= entitlements.keyword_tracking_refresh_days == 1 ? "Daily" : "Weekly" %> refresh
  <% if estimate %>
    &middot; Next run <%= estimate.human %>
  <% end %>
  <% if paused_count > 0 %>
    &middot; <span class="text-warning/80"><%= paused_count %> paused</span>
    &mdash;
    <%= link_to "Upgrade to resume", pricing_path, class: "text-primary/70 underline" %>
  <% end %>
  <% unless entitlements.apple_ads_integration_enabled? %>
    &middot; <span class="text-primary/60"><%= link_to "Upgrade to unlock popularity data", pricing_path, class: "underline" %></span>
  <% end %>
</div>
